# =============================================================================
# json — a bare identifier is not a JSON value
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • JSON values are strings, numbers, objects, arrays and the wire words
#     `true`, `false` and `null`.
#   • A bare identifier such as `foo` is not JSON data and is rejected while
#     parsing the JSON literal.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Writing `{ "flag": foo }` when a JSON boolean was meant — write `true`.
#   • Expecting a Faber binding to be resolved inside a JSON literal.
#
# See also: json
# =============================================================================

main { let json a ← { "flag": foo } ; print a }
